# perf/ k6 load tests -- reports are per-run artifacts, not source
perf/reports/

# Agent / editor tooling. These are per-machine working state, not part of
# the project: .claude/ alone is 108 files of a vendored skill plus a
# settings.local.json that only makes sense on this machine.
.claude/
.impeccable/
.remember/

# Markdown is tracked. There used to be a blanket `*.md` here with a single
# `!README.md` escape, which silently swallowed every document the project
# actually wants under version control -- docs/, perf/README.md and
# Front-end/DESIGN_HANDOFF.md were all invisible to `git add`. Ignore the
# scratch files by name instead, so a new document is tracked by default and
# dropping one takes a deliberate line here.
